WEBVTT

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.970
I'd like to see James.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.490
I'd like to visit the SSC.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:35.450
Oh, in that case...

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.950
He doesn't know I'm here.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:40.580
So...

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.500
I wanted to drop in to surprise him.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.630
What floor is the SSC on?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.350
Could you let me through the gate?

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.060
You have a nice face.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.020
Maybe you could model for me sometime.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:12.820
What's the trouble?

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.650
Amazing.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.440
Just simply amazing!

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.470
What is happening?

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:21.890
That guy!

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:23.720
James!

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:00.130
You.

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:05.470
James!

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:08.390
James, James, James!

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.470
Is that you, Grimm?

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:15.890
I came all this way for you.
Aren't you happy to see me?

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.400
You're supposed to be dead.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.030
I just had to see you again,
so I came back from the dead.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.030
And it's finally happening.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.170
What?

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:58.600
James, you give me inspiration.

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.020
This is a strange sight, isn't it?

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.110
Can you believe it?

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.460
A GPS round, huh?

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.590
This is how you caught me three years ago.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.470
Isn't it?

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:28.930
What?

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.590
What is that?

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:12.220
Yes, yes, yes! That's the face!

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.800
Oh, how I've dreamed of this.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.850
This day is finally here.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:41.870
Sarah!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.630
Why must you interfere with my process?

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.910
Oh, ouch.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.120
That hurts, you know?

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.160
What's going on?

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.420
What?

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.500
What is this?

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:43.730
There he is!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.760
What are you doing here, Sarah?

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.090
I got caught in the crossfire downstairs.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.470
But I felt I had to go after him.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.310
Why would you do something so reckless?

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.730
This was hidden in Monica's room.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:41.990
He had the same thing.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.440
My God...

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.230
The attacker was Grimm?

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:17.320
He died in prison. You should know that,
since you arrested him.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.370
But it was definitely him.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:24.410
Three years ago...

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:29.540
Grimm's arrest was big news,
even among the prosecutors.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:32.790
I wouldn't mistake that face.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.010
You, too, huh?

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:43.050
So, this allows him to change his face.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:46.180
And...

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:50.350
this was hidden in Monica's room.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.070
Masks...

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.800
<i>After finding these pictures</i>

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.260
and witnessing what I saw...

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:05.050
I believe Monica's death
wasn't due to heart failure.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.390
Grimm had the same mask.

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:11.980
He's our best lead
for finding out what happened.

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.950
Sarah, would you leave this to us?

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:28.080
This case has too many unknowns.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.290
I want to avoid putting you in danger.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:36.290
Of course, we would report all our
findings, including Monica's case, to you.

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.130
I'd like you to leave this to the SSC.

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:19.540
Yes...

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.510
Red...

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:26.880
I need real red!

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.580
Come, James! Yes, come!

00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:59.630
A GPS round just activated
a few moments ago.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:06.130
<i>James!</i>

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:13.180
It's late.

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.520
I'll have someone take you home.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.690
We can talk more tomorrow.

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:26.150
Eddy. Send the coordinates to the car.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:47.090
I'm coming with you.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.430
So, this is where he is.

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:51.970
<i>Sarah.</i>

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.720
You need to leave this to James.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:56.220
Sarah.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.690
I want to find out the truth
behind Monica's death.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:15.660
I used to get myself
into a lot of trouble.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:19.960
<i>But then Gallagher took me in.</i>

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:24.090
<i>Monica would help</i>
<i>when I was particularly bad.</i>

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:30.050
Back then, Monica was like a mother to me.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:32.590
And I was a constant headache to her.

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:36.260
She often talked about you.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:46.690
I thought it'd be here.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:50.190
James, don't do anything reckless.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.530
<i>Sarah will stay in the car.</i>

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:05.590
That son of a bitch.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:15.140
Backup is on the way.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.100
Run if something happens.

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:19.810
Got it?

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.440
We can get some answers
after he's captured.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:28.820
You're going in alone?

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:33.200
He's only after me.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.730
That piece is almost finished.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:55.530
<i>Do you remember this place?</i>

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:59.530
Yes, it's where I arrested you.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:01.490
Oh, how wonderful.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.040
I'm so happy that you remembered.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.750
And I'm going to capture you here again.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.170
That's not an option for me.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.930
Yes, that's the look.

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:23.640
What is that thing?

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:25.270
Grimm!

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:28.560
James!

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.700
Shouldn't you be aiming here?

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:18.900
This is exactly how I imagined it.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:24.030
I owe a debt of gratitude to this.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.450
What is that Mask?

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:31.120
I need it to complete this painting.

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:33.960
You understand, don't you, James?

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:36.460
I'm asking you what that Mask is!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.960
It's your blood, James. Your blood!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:43.720
This painting will finally be complete
with your blood!

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.800
Yes, this is the feeling.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.090
Now...

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:25.010
Finally...

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:50.240
Grimm.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.750
James.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.510
-Grimm?
-Yes.

00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:11.220
I know it's hard to believe,
but this is Grimm.

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:16.350
We still have questions for you.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:18.190
Right?

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.390
A colleague who had photographs
of this Mask died.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.390
What is this thing?

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.440
I'm...

00:21:57.730 --> 00:22:00.150
I'm just a guinea pig.

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:11.620
Damn it.

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.090
What's the situation?

00:22:22.590 --> 00:22:23.920
We recovered two bodies.

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:26.380
But we also lost two on our side.

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:31.470
The SSC are aware of the Masks.

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:34.350
Just perfect.

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:36.850
Who can we thank for that?

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:42.360
Grimm.

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:21.960
Subtitle translation by Zensho Yamamoto
